      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "Karlin et al. (1979) show that, under polygenic inheritance with additive loci, offspring more closely resemble the average of their parents (the midparent) than either individual parent, whereas the converse is true when a major gene is segregating. Exploiting this relationship, they proposed a class of indices for indicating the presence of major genes,",
